Auto Care Association releases 2026 Auto Care Factbook report detailing steady growth in the global aftermarket industry despite recent economic and trade uncertainties.

BETHESDA, Md. – June 13, 2025 – The Auto Care Association today released its annual automotive aftermarket industry reports, the 2026 Auto Care Factbook and the 2026 A uto Care Factbook & Lang Annual . These award-winning and industry-leading reports are the go-to source for automotive aftermarket industry data that provides the critical insight aftermarket businesses need to make data-driven decisions for the future. The 35th edition of the Auto Care Factbook report provides an all-encompassing view of the aftermarket industry, including new operational insights for navigating the evolving trade and tariffs policy landscape for 2025 and beyond.

The auto care industry grew robustly in 2024, in line with expectations. Despite continued challenges throughout the economy including inflation, along with uncertainties as new trade and government policies emerged, the aftermarket demonstrated resilience, with total United States light duty aftermarket sales growing by 5.7% in 2024 to $413.7 billion – in line with the previous year’s projections of 5.9%. Continued steady growth is expected for the light duty aftermarket in 2025 at 5.1%, with the total light, medium and heavy duty automotive aftermarket now expected to be a $664.3 billion industry in 2028.

