The 2026 Auto Care Factbook also provides Auto Care Association members exclusive access to nearly 50 economic and industry indicators through the association’s Auto Care TrendLens™ interactive data platform. Using the TrendLens™ platform, members can view up-to-date data, as well as filter and overlay with other data sets to gain a more complete view of the industry and its current trends.

“We are proud to present the 35th version of the Auto Care Factbook , a resource that is valued around the world for its insights into our industry. This year’s edition highlights that the U.S. automotive aftermarket industry has demonstrated remarkable resilience, showing steady year-over-year growth—even amid global supply chain disruptions and rising inflation,” said Bill Hanvey, president and CEO, Auto Care Association. “The auto care industry reached $414 billion in 2024 and is projected to surpass $664 billion by 2028. This consistent expansion reflects the essential nature of vehicle maintenance and repair, as America’s more than 239 million licensed drivers increasingly choose to extend the life of their vehicles—now averaging over 12.8 years on the road—rather than replace them.”

The 2026 Auto Care Factbook & Lang Annual report includes the Auto Care Factbook plus the Lang Annual , which provides a supplemental, comprehensive overview of the U.S. light vehicle aftermarket and presents information and analysis available from no other source.

All Auto Care Association contacts at member companies receive a complimentary digital copy of the 2026 Auto Care Factbook report as an association member benefit. The non-member price for the publication is $2,950. The Auto Care Factbook & Lang Annual report can be purchased for $1,095 for members and $4,045 for non-members.

To order any of these digital publications, please visit autocare.org/factbook or contact the Member Services department at publications@autocare.org or 301-654-6664.
